---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Lesson 8: Ultrasonic Sensors and Distance Measurement - C00lnerd Tutoring">
    <div style="max-width: 1000px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem;">
        
            <!-- Header -->
            <div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #667eea 0%, #764ba2 100%); color: white; padding: 3rem; border-radius: 15px; margin-bottom: 2rem; text-align: center;">
                <h1 style="font-size: 2.5rem; font-weight: bold; margin: 0 0 1rem 0;">Week 8: Ultrasonic Sensors and Distance Measurement</h1>
                <p style="font-size: 1.2rem; margin: 0; opacity: 0.9;">Measure distance and detect obstacles using ultrasonic sensors</p>
                <div class="mt-4 p-4 bg-cyan-100 rounded-lg">
                    <p class="text-cyan-800 font-medium">📡 From output devices to sensors - giving robots spatial awareness</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Learning Objectives -->
            <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg p-8 mb-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-cyan-800 mb-6">📚 Learning Objectives</h2>
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem; margin-bottom: 2rem;">
                    <div>
                        <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center;">By the end of this lesson, you will:</h3>
                        <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                <span class="text-cyan-600 mr-2">•</span>
                                Understand ultrasonic sensor principles and operation
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                <span class="text-cyan-600 mr-2">•</span>
                                Measure distances accurately using HC-SR04 sensors
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                <span class="text-cyan-600 mr-2">•</span>
                                Implement obstacle detection and avoidance systems
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                <span class="text-cyan-600 mr-2">•</span>
                                Combine sensors with output devices for feedback
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem; display: flex; align-items: center;">Key Concepts:</h3>
                        <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                <span class="text-cyan-600 mr-2">•</span>
                                Sound waves and time-of-flight measurement
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                <span class="text-cyan-600 mr-2">•</span>
                                Trigger and echo signal timing
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                <span class="text-cyan-600 mr-2">•</span>
                                Distance calculation and calibration
                            </li>
                            <li style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
                                <span class="text-cyan-600 mr-2">•</span>
                                Sensor fusion and decision making
                            </li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Section 1: Ultrasonic Sensor Fundamentals -->
            <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-lg p-8 mb-8">
                <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-cyan-800 mb-6">🔊 Section 1: Ultrasonic Sensor Fundamentals</h2>
                
                <div style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                    <h3 style="color: #2d3748; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">How Ultrasonic Sensors Work</h3>
                    <p style="color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.6; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
                        Ultrasonic sensors use high-frequency sound waves to measure distance. They work like 
                        sonar systems - sending out sound pulses and measuring the time for echoes to return.
                    </p>
                    
                    <div style="background: #edf2f7; padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                        <h4 style="color: #2d3748; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 1rem;">HC-SR04 Specifications:</h4>
                        <ul style="list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; color: #4a5568; line-height: 1.8;">
                            <li><strong>Range:</strong> 2cm to 400cm</li>
                            <li><strong>Accuracy:</strong> ±3mm</li>
                            <li><strong>Frequency:</strong> 40kHz ultrasonic</li>
                            <li><strong>Distance Formula:</strong> Distance = (Time × 0.0343) ÷ 2</li>
                        </ul>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Navigation -->
            <div class="flex justify-between items-center mt-8">
                <div>
                    <a href="/programming/lessons32/week7" style="background-color: #6b7280; color: white; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; border: 2px solid #4b5563; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); transition: all 0.2s; display: inline-block;" onmouseover="this.style.backgroundColor='#4b5563'; this.style.transform='translateY(-2px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'" onmouseout="this.style.backgroundColor='#6b7280'; this.style.transform='translateY(0px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'">
                        ← Previous: Week 7
                    </a>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <a href="/programming/" style="background-color: #059669; color: white; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; border: 2px solid #047857; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); transition: all 0.2s; display: inline-block;" onmouseover="this.style.backgroundColor='#047857'; this.style.transform='translateY(-2px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'" onmouseout="this.style.backgroundColor='#059669'; this.style.transform='translateY(0px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'">
                        Course Overview
                    </a>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <a href="/programming/lessons32/week9" style="background-color: #2563eb; color: white; padding: 12px 20px; border-radius: 8px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; border: 2px solid #1d4ed8; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); transition: all 0.2s; display: inline-block;" onmouseover="this.style.backgroundColor='#1d4ed8'; this.style.transform='translateY(-2px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 10px 15px -3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'" onmouseout="this.style.backgroundColor='#2563eb'; this.style.transform='translateY(0px)'; this.style.boxShadow='0 4px 6px -1px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1)'">
                        Next: Week 9 →
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>
